30,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"It seems people are wasting an hour a day copying records, and misrouted deliveries are happening because of inconsistent addresses.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,May,,Our developers are tied up until Q3 and the coordination group is understaffed. We can't just add more work to them.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Network coverage at plants is terrible, and visitor approval takes forever. Also, per-head licensing is a trap for scaling.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The capital budget is frozen, but we have software allowance. Also, we are asking vendors for the same certificates repeatedly.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Past projects that required everyone to enter data failed, but narrow tools for specific trades actually survived!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Ryuji, if the capital budget is frozen, does that mean we can only afford software-based solutions?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, that's a huge warning. If a proposal requires everyone to use it daily, it'll probably fail.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, combined with the developer shortage, any complex build is a risk. We need something lean.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Yes, Daisuke, we are limited to the recurring software allowance. We must avoid any heavy capital expenditure.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Kenji,,Exactly! We should look for something that helps a specific group rather than a forced company-wide habit.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,The data duplication and address errors are real daily losses. We need a solution for that.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,May,,"But who will manage it? If the coordination group is already drowning, a new system might just be a burden.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"And if it's for field work, the network issues I found make a mobile app very risky.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The vendor query issue suggests we have a fragmented way of handling supplier data.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"That sounds like a standardization effort, which I found often end up without an owner.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
