55,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The candidates are A, B, C, and D. I think C, the Supplier Data Hub, addresses the address and record issues.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,May,,A requires field use and D requires daily entry from everyone. Both sound like nightmares for staffing and adoption.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,I agree. A is dead because of the network coverage and visitor approvals. D is too broad.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,C fits the software allowance and solves the redundant vendor queries I discovered.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Kenji,,B is a narrow tool for skill transfer. That fits the pattern of what actually survives!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, B is nice, but C stops the actual errors in deliveries. That's a more urgent daily loss.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, would C require too much from the coordination group to set up?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"C is a repository. If it's a fixed-fee build, it avoids the license trap and the developer shortage.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,It should be manageable if we use the software allowance for a vendor-hosted hub.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"I see the point, but B doesn't require any daily data entry from the masses. It's safer.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I still feel C is the most helpful for the people on the floor.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,May,,I'm leaning towards B or C. D is definitely out.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,C is the most rational choice to fix the fragmented data without relying on plant networks.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I support C. It solves the budget constraint and the vendor redundancy.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"If everyone wants C, I can't argue, but I still worry about the ownership of standardization.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for C.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,May,,I'll go with C as well.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,C for me.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,C.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'll vote B, just to be safe, but C has the momentum.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
